      "id": "md2025_2286",
      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "Compare the forward-looking statement language in Item 7 of LLY and PFE for fiscal years 2022 and 2024. What specific wording change occurs for LLY between the two years, and how does PFE's language remain consistent? Additionally, based on the common structure of MD&A, which financial statement line item (commonly found in the financial tables) would an analyst use to quantify the risk associated with the forward-looking statements about 'cash generated from operations'?",
      "expected_answer": "LLY's 2022 Item 7 text includes the phrase 'differ materially from these forward-looking statements', while the 2024 text omits 'materially' and states 'differ from these forward-looking statements'. PFE's Item 7 text is identical in both 2022 and 2024, using the standard 'MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS...' opening without any variation. To quantify the risk for 'cash generated from operations', an analyst would refer to the Statement of Cash Flows in the financial tables, specifically the line 'Net cash provided by operating activities'.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** LLY removed the word \"materially\" from its forward-looking caution in FY2024, while PFE's language remained verbatim across both years. An analyst would use **Net cash provided by operating activities** (or equivalent) from the **Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows** to quantify risk around \"cash generated from operations.\"\n\n- **LLY FY2022:** \"may cause our actual results, financial position, and cash generated from operations to differ **materially** from these forward-looking statements\" [E1]\n- **LLY FY2024:** \"may cause our actual results, financial position, and cash generated from operations to differ from these forward-looking statements\" [E2]\n- **PFE FY2022 & FY2024:** Identical introductory clause: \"including an evaluation of the amounts and certainty of cash flows from operations and from outside sources\" [E3][E4]\n\nThe specific LLY change is the deletion of \"materially\" before \"differ.\" PFE's consistency is shown by the exact repetition of its MD&A General opening, which embeds forward-looking concepts within the analytical purpose statement rather than using a separate safe-harbor caution.\n\n**Sources:**\n[E1] LLY_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Results of Operations and Financial Condition\n[E2] LLY_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Results of Operations and Financial Condition\n[E3] PFE_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E4] PFE_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations",
